.\" jarvisagent(1) — JarvisAgent user manual
.\" Generated for JarvisAgent 0.8
.TH JARVISAGENT 1 "March 2026" "JarvisAgent 0.8" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
jarvisAgent \- parallel AI\-driven automation engine with visual workflow editor
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jarvisAgent
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
JarvisAgent is a C++ backend / React frontend application for parallel
AI\-driven automation.
Its engine core dispatches many concurrent AI requests in parallel \(em think
requirements analysis across hundreds of items, stock\-portfolio deep\-research
across every position, or chapter\-by\-chapter processing of entire PDF books.
.PP
Office documents (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, PDF) are automatically converted to
Markdown via Microsoft MarkItDown \(em and chunked when too large \(em before
being sent to the AI.
JarvisAgent is file\-oriented by design: all inputs, outputs, and intermediate
results live on disk, making it a natural fit for engineering environments with
large file landscapes.
.PP
Workflows let you chain serial and parallel tasks \(em AI calls, Python scripts,
shell commands, or native C++ \(em in a visual graph editor with various trigger
types (manual, cron, file_watch).
.PP
The application ships with an ncurses terminal UI for local or SSH sessions,
a browser\-based React dashboard for remote monitoring, and a visual workflow
editor.
It compiles and runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
.PP
When no TTY is detected (e.g. inside a Docker container without
.BR \-it ),
JarvisAgent automatically runs in headless mode: the ncurses TUI and keyboard
input are disabled, but the web server, REST API, and WebSocket interface
remain fully functional.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print the version number and exit.
.PP
Unknown options cause an error message and a non\-zero exit code.
.
