.SH CONFIGURATION
JarvisAgent reads
.B config.json
from the current working directory at startup.
If the file is missing, the application prints an error and exits.
.PP
The following fields are recognized:
.TP
.B "file format identifier"
(number) Internal format version for the config file.
.TP
.B "description"
(string) A human\-readable description of this configuration.
.TP
.B "author"
(string) Author or owner of this configuration.
.TP
.B "queue folder"
(string, \fBrequired\fR) Relative or absolute path to the queue directory.
JarvisAgent monitors this folder for incoming files that trigger AI requests.
.TP
.B "workflows folder"
(string) Relative or absolute path to the directory containing
.B .jcwf
workflow definition files.
Defaults to
.IR workflows/ .
.TP
.B "max threads"
(number) Maximum number of concurrent AI request threads.
.TP
.B "engine sleep time in run loop in ms"
(number) Main loop sleep duration in milliseconds.
Controls CPU usage vs. responsiveness.
.TP
.B "max file size in kB"
(number) Maximum input file size in kilobytes.
Files larger than this are chunked before being sent to the AI.
Default: 20.
.TP
.B "verbose"
(boolean) Enable verbose logging output.
.TP
.B "keys_file"
(string) Path to the encrypted API keys file.
Default:
.IR keys.json.enc .
See
.B ENVIRONMENT
below.
.TP
.B "API index"
(number) Zero\-based index of the default AI interface to use from the
.B "API interfaces"
array.
.TP
.B "API interfaces"
(array) List of AI provider configurations.
Each entry is an object with the following fields:
.RS
.TP
.B url
(string, \fBrequired\fR) The API endpoint URL
(e.g. \fIhttps://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions\fR).
.TP
.B model
(string) The model name (e.g. \fIgpt\-4o\fR, \fIgemini\-2.5\-flash\fR).
.TP
.B API
(string) The reply parser type: \fBAPI1\fR (OpenAI\-compatible) or \fBAPI2\fR.
.TP
.B name
(string) Human\-readable name for this interface.
Auto\-generated from URL domain + model if omitted.
.TP
.B description
(string) Optional description of this interface.
.TP
.B key_name
(string) Name of the API key provider to use from the encrypted keys file
(e.g. "openai", "google", "anthropic").
.RE
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JARVIS_MASTER_PASSWORD
Master password for decrypting the encrypted API keys file
.RB ( keys.json.enc ).
When this variable is set, JarvisAgent decrypts the keys file automatically
at startup without prompting.
This is especially useful for Docker containers and CI environments.
The master password is never stored on disk.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Backward\-compatible fallback.
If no encrypted keys file is found and this variable is set, JarvisAgent
creates a single "openai" provider entry using the key value.
This is a convenience for simple single\-provider setups.
.PP
API key priority order:
.IP 1. 4
Encrypted keys file
.RB ( keys.json.enc )
decrypted with
.BR JARVIS_MASTER_PASSWORD .
.IP 2.
Plaintext keys file
.RB ( keys.json )
\(em development fallback only.
.IP 3.
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
environment variable.
.
.SH AI SETUP
To use AI\-powered workflows, you need at least one API key configured.
.SS Setting up API keys
.IP 1. 4
Open the workflow editor at \fIhttp://localhost:8080/editor\fR.
.IP 2.
Navigate to the \fBSettings\fR page (gear icon) and select \fBAI Keys\fR.
.IP 3.
Add a provider name (e.g. "openai", "google", "anthropic") and paste the
corresponding API key.
.IP 4.
Click \fBSave Encrypted\fR.
You will be prompted for a master password.
This encrypts all keys into
.B keys.json.enc
in the working directory.
.SS Setting up AI models
.IP 1. 4
In the workflow editor, navigate to the \fBAI Manager\fR page.
.IP 2.
Configure one or more AI interfaces: set the API endpoint URL, model name,
parser type (API1 for OpenAI\-compatible, API2 for native), and select which
key provider to use.
.IP 3.
Set the default interface index or override per\-task in workflow definitions.
.PP
Supported providers include OpenAI, Google Gemini (via the OpenAI\-compatible
endpoint), Anthropic, and any provider offering an OpenAI\-compatible chat
completions API.
.
.SH WORKFLOWS
JarvisAgent uses
.B JC Workflow
definition files
.RB ( .jcwf )
to describe automation pipelines as directed acyclic graphs (DAGs).
.PP
A workflow consists of:
.IP \(bu 3
\fBTasks\fR \(em individual units of work: AI calls, shell commands, Python
scripts, or internal actions.
Tasks can run in parallel when their dependencies allow it.
.IP \(bu
\fBEdges\fR \(em dependency and dataflow connections between tasks.
A task only runs after all its upstream dependencies have completed.
.IP \(bu
\fBTriggers\fR \(em how a workflow is started: manually, on a cron schedule,
or when a file appears in a watched directory.
.IP \(bu
\fBFilters\fR \(em per\-item expansion from CSV files, text line lists, or
queries.
A single task definition can fan out into many parallel instances.
.PP
Task types:
.TP
.B ai_call
Send a prompt (with optional file attachments) to an AI provider and capture
the response.
.TP
.B shell
Run a shell command or script.
Stdout and stderr are captured.
.TP
.B python
Call a Python function with structured inputs/outputs.
.TP
.B internal
Built\-in actions (e.g. file operations).
.PP
For the full specification including JSON schema, dataflow mapping, template
syntax, filter types, and per\-item expansion, see:
.PP
.RS
.B doc/JC_Workflow_Specification.md
.RE
.
.SH WORKFLOW EDITOR
The visual workflow editor is a React application served by JarvisAgent at:
.PP
.RS
\fIhttp://localhost:8080/editor\fR
.RE
.PP
Key features:
.IP \(bu 3
\fBVisual DAG editor\fR \(em drag\-and\-drop nodes, draw dependency and
dataflow edges between tasks.
.IP \(bu
\fBTask inspector\fR \(em configure task type, parameters, file inputs/outputs,
working directory, timeout, and per\-task AI interface override.
.IP \(bu
\fBWorkflow CRUD\fR \(em open, save, validate, run, and clean workflows.
.IP \(bu
\fBLive run monitoring\fR \(em task state badges update in real time via
WebSocket (running, succeeded, failed, skipped).
.IP \(bu
\fBRun controls\fR \(em start, stop, pause, and resume workflow runs.
.IP \(bu
\fBTemplate browser\fR \(em start from pre\-built workflow templates.
.IP \(bu
\fBValidation\fR \(em the backend validates the workflow structure and
reports issues with severity tiers directly on the canvas.
.IP \(bu
\fBFilter builder\fR \(em configure CSV, text_lines, or query filters
for per\-item fan\-out.
.IP \(bu
\fBLog viewer\fR \(em virtual\-scrolling log display with search and
run analysis (see
.B DASHBOARD
below for details).
.
.SH DASHBOARD
The React dashboard is served at:
.PP
.RS
\fIhttp://localhost:8080\fR
.RE
.PP
It has two tabs: a \fBDashboard\fR overview and a \fBLog Viewer\fR.
.SS Dashboard tab
.IP \(bu 3
\fBStatus bar\fR \(em live WebSocket connection indicator, active workflow
runs, AI session count, completed/failed counters, and a quit button.
.IP \(bu
\fBWorkflows panel\fR \(em lists all registered workflows with controls to
run or clean each workflow.
.IP \(bu
\fBSession managers panel\fR \(em shows active AI request sessions with
real\-time status updates.
.SS Log Viewer tab
A full\-screen, virtual\-scrolling log display (up to 100\,000 lines).
.IP \(bu 3
\fBLive streaming\fR \(em new log lines arrive in real time via WebSocket.
.IP \(bu
\fBAuto\-scroll\fR \(em follows the latest output; toggles between
\fBFollow\fR and \fBPaused\fR mode.
Click the button or scroll up to pause, click again to resume.
.IP \(bu
\fBSearch\fR \(em press \fB/\fR or \fBCtrl+F\fR to search.
Navigate matches with \fBEnter\fR (next) / \fBShift+Enter\fR (previous).
Match count and position are shown in the toolbar.
.IP \(bu
\fBColor\-coded log levels\fR \(em lines containing \fC[error]\fR are
displayed in \fBred\fR; lines containing \fC[warning]\fR or \fC[warn]\fR
are displayed in \fByellow\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBRun Analyzer\fR \(em press \fB1\fR or click the \fBAnalyze\fR button.
An overlay panel appears showing:
.RS
.IP \(en 3
Workflow ID, run ID, state, start/end timestamps.
.IP \(en
Clickable log\-region links (start line \(em end line) to jump directly
to the run\(aqs output.
.IP \(en
\fB\(la\fR / \fB\(ra\fR arrows to cycle through previous runs
(newest first).
.IP \(en
\fBIssues list\fR \(em all warnings and errors within the run, color\-coded
by severity (red for errors, yellow for warnings).
.IP \(en
\fB\(ua\fR / \fB\(da\fR arrows to step through issues one by one; clicking
an issue jumps to its log line.
.RE
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config.json
Main configuration file (must exist in the working directory).
.TP
.B keys.json.enc
Encrypted API keys (AES\-256, master\-password protected).
.TP
.B keys.json
Plaintext API keys (development fallback, gitignored).
.TP
.B workflows/
Directory containing
.B .jcwf
workflow definition files.
.TP
.B queue/
Monitored directory for incoming files.
.TP
.B log/log.txt
Application log file.
.TP
.B .venv/
Python virtual environment (auto\-created by launcher scripts).
Contains markitdown, md2pdf\-mermaid, and playwright.
.
